binary, which the engine's packaging step does for you.

## Third-party components

like-nes links third-party libraries that remain under their own licenses.
Those licenses are **not** superseded by this file — when you redistribute a
binary you must satisfy them too. All of them are permissive and compatible
with both arms above; the full inventory, including which arm of each
dual-licensed dependency this project elects, is in
[`THIRD-PARTY.md`](THIRD-PARTY.md), and their verbatim notices are in
[`THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt`](THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt),
[`THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES-RUST.txt`](THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES-RUST.txt) and
[`THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES-NDK.txt`](THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES-NDK.txt).

